/*
 * session — the state of the compilations of a workspace.
 *
 * The configuration of a compilation (`global::state`) and its diagnostics
 * (`errors::diagnostic`) are per thread, and reset between two compilations.
 * A language server compiles several workspaces from the same threads, each
 * with its own configuration: a Session keeps the one of a workspace, and
 * installs it for the length of a compilation (cf. `Parser::inSession`),
 * restoring the one of the thread afterwards. Its compilations run one at a
 * time, whatever the thread. It also keeps the syntax trees of the files it
 * read, reused while they do not change, and the token its latest compilation
 * can be cancelled through.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::session
 * @File: ymirc/session.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-10-01
